# Fetch Data at Build Time

`getStaticProps` is a special **async function** you export from a page file. Next.js calls it:

* **At build time** (production).
* On the server (never in the browser).
* It returns props that are passed to your page component.

```jsx
export async function getStaticProps() {
  const data = await fetch('https://api.example.com/posts');
  return { props: { data } };
}
```

The page will be **pre‑rendered** with the fetched data – ready to ship! 📦

slides.codeSnippet:
// pages/posts.js
export default function Posts({ posts }) {
  return (
    <ul>
      {posts.map(post => <li key={post.id}>{post.title}</li>)}
    </ul>
  );
}

export async function getStaticProps() {
  const res = await fetch('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts');
  const posts = await res.json();
  return { props: { posts } };
}

slides.content:
# What getStaticProps Must Return

```js
return {
  props: { ... },   // required – passed to page component
  revalidate: 60,   // optional – enable ISR (seconds)
  notFound: true,   // optional – show 404 page
  redirect: {       // optional – redirect to another URL
    destination: '/new',
    permanent: false
  }
};
```

At minimum, you need `props`. Everything else is optional superpowers!

slides.codeSnippet:
// pages/product.js
export default function Product({ product }) {
  return <h1>{product.name}</h1>;
}

export async function getStaticProps() {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/product/123');
  if (res.status === 404) {
    return { notFound: true };
  }
  const product = await res.json();
  return { props: { product } };
}
